This repository is dual-licensed, separating code from data.

  Code    scripts/, site/, examples/,       MIT          see LICENSE-MIT
          src/
  Data    catalog.json, retired.json,       CC0-1.0      see LICENSE-CC0
          schema/, docs/, README*.md

The published `awesome-jev-mcp` package is that MIT code plus a snapshot of the
CC0 data files, which it carries only as an offline last resort. Both licences
travel in the wheel, and neither changes by being installed.

Rows in catalog.json carry a per-row `license` field. Every row in the current
build is CC0-1.0. A row whose descriptive text was inherited from a CC BY 4.0
source carries `CC-BY-4.0` instead, and its attribution is that row's `sources`
array.

Works linked FROM this catalog remain under their own licences. The
`repo_license` field on a row records what the linked project declares, which is
not always what its README badge claims. Rows flagged `no-license` link to
projects that ship no LICENSE file at all — check before reusing their code.

See docs/sources.md for the full licence position.
